prompt:
Use the supplied Nova Stitch gameplay sprite as the identity/style reference. Create an original 1536×1024 transparent RGBA sprite sheet with exactly ten separate complete full-body Nova Stitch controlled fall-and-recovery poses in a five-column by two-row grid, row-major. Use one distinct connected pose in every cell. Consistent right-facing source direction, camera, scale and anatomy. No scene, floor, shadow, background, prop, text, basketball, teammate or opponent.

Nova is a young athletic fair-tan woman with long curly teal hair in a high ponytail, distinct human face, teal jersey and shorts with purple/black trim, black knee pads, teal-black sneakers and wristbands. Preserve her face, human proportions, ponytail, uniform palette and shoes in all poses. Do not depict another person. This is a brief game knockdown and recovery, not an injury: no gore, no impact effects, no broken limbs, no crawling locomotion. Her body moves through one intentional fall and then stands back up.

Ten connected poses:
0 balance disrupted, torso leans and arms widen;
1 take an off-balance step and bend knees;
2 begin a controlled backward/side descent, hands reach to brace;
3 lower onto one knee and forearm;
4 controlled low seated/side-fall, legs bent naturally;
5 brief grounded recovery pose on one knee and hand, complete body visible;
6 plant both hands/one foot to rise;
7 lift torso into a low squat;
8 stand gradually and regain balance;
9 return to a normal upright right-facing ready stance.
The central ground-contact poses are intentional recovery, not a normal running pose. Keep limbs anatomically correct and non-overlapping, all hair and shoes visible within each cell, and the face fully identifiable when angle permits.

Match the supplied tiny 2D arcade sprite: crisp limited-palette 1990s pixel art with chunky dark outlines, not painterly, photorealistic, 3D, glossy or anime. True RGBA alpha-zero outside cells, no floor shadow, glow, matte or checkerboard. Return only the sprite sheet.
